      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The curves meet where \\( 3 y^{2} = \\frac{5 y}{2} + \\frac{1}{2} \\), at \\( y = 1 \\), and the region runs from the x-axis, \\( y = 0 \\), up to there. On that interval the line is to the right of the parabola.",
         "rule_named": "limits in y and the right-hand curve"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The area is \\( \\int_{0}^{1} \\left(\\left(\\frac{5 y}{2} + \\frac{1}{2}\\right) - \\left(3 y^{2}\\right)\\right)\\,dy = \\frac{3}{4} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
